#### Job Description

Data professional with an analytical profile and business vision, capable of transforming CRM data into actionable insights and applying analytics and artificial intelligence techniques to optimize acquisition, retention and customer relationship strategies.

Proactive professional, results-oriented and with a strong sense of ownership, capable of acting strategically and executively in the evolution of data-driven CRM.

Main responsibilities

- Design and build data solutions for CRM, structuring datasets, tables, rules and pipelines that support campaigns, journeys and customer relationship strategies;
- Develop segmentations and customer intelligence at scale, transforming business rules and needs into automated, reusable and productive data solutions;
- Evolve the CRM data architecture, contributing with modeling, integration, performance, quality, observability and governance of data;
- Develop and put into production data products and services that can be reliably consumed by CRM and other teams in the company;
- Build solutions using SQL, Python and Databricks, seeking automation, efficiency, scalability and reduction of manual processes;
- Apply AI Engineering and GenAI concepts to develop automations, agents, tools and solutions that facilitate access to data, insights and knowledge;
- Create mechanisms for democratizing data and knowledge, reducing dependence on manual analyses and enabling business areas to have greater autonomy;
- Work with stakeholders to transform business problems into technical requirements, data solutions and measurable hypotheses;
- Develop proofs of value, experiments and measurement mechanisms that allow assessing the impact of solutions and supporting data-based decisions;
- Ensure good practices of documentation, versioning, testing, monitoring and maintenance of the solutions developed;
- Take ownership of your deliverables, performing estimates, planning, scope and deadline negotiation, risk identification and progress reports for stakeholders.

#### Qualifications

**Expected knowledge and skills:**

- Advanced SQL, including manipulation and transformation of large volumes of data;
- Databricks, with experience in developing and operationalizing data solutions;
- Python applied to engineering, automation, processing and data analysis;
- Knowledge of data engineering, including pipelines, ETL/ELT, modeling, integration and data quality;
- Knowledge of AI/GenAI Engineering, including building and integrating solutions based on LLMs, automations and agents;
- Ability to develop solutions with production, scalability, reliability and reuse in mind, not just one-off analyses;
- Good ability to connect technical decisions to business objectives and results;
- Clear communication and ability to move between technical and business stakeholders;
- Autonomy, organization, estimation skills and management of one's own deliverables.

**Differentials**

- Experience with CRM, Customer Analytics, segmentation and customer activation, experimentation/A-B testing, APIs, Git/CI/CD, Lakehouse architecture, Delta Lake, MLflow and development of AI solutions integrated into corporate environments.

  We seek, above all, someone who can combine Engineering + Data + Intelligence + Business: a person capable of understanding a problem, designing the solution, building it, putting it into production and demonstrating the value generated.


