We are evolving our BU from a model centred on isolated products to an architecture of platforms and reusable components, which supports critical solutions used by major banks, cooperatives, and companies across many sectors.

In this context, we are looking for a Tech Lead Specialist to be the technical reference for a software development squad. This person will have the autonomy to decide and prioritise the technical implementations that enter the downstream and will be responsible for creating the conditions for the squad to perform: with quality, predictability, and autonomy in its own deliveries.

We are looking for an AI Native profile, someone who already uses artificial intelligence in their daily engineering work, applies these techniques in the squad's development cycle, and empowers the team to do the same, with real productivity gains and without compromising quality or security.

**Main Responsibilities:**

- Be the technical reference for the squad and the demand flow: technical triage, unblocking the team, standards, and quality;
- Maintain the technical coherence of what the squad delivers: standards, quality, security, and maintainability;
- Promote the team's technical autonomy: document, delegate, and create criteria so the team can make good decisions without depending on you;
- Ensure that local decisions respect the architecture and the platform, or challenge them consciously, with technical rationale;
- Provide visibility of risks and technical options to the Tech Manager and PM in advance, before they become problems;
- Lead the adoption of AI in the squad: learn, apply, and train the team in AI-assisted engineering techniques;
- Work on observability and monitoring of services, ensuring minimum instrumentation (logs, metrics, and traces) and actionable alerts;
- Channel your dissatisfaction with underperforming processes into effective changes within the team and the company.

**What a Day Looks Like:**

- Lead technical discussions, guide implementation, and raise the engineering standard of the team day to day;
- Review PRs with a focus on risk, quality, and maintainability, and train the team to reduce their dependence on you;
- Map the team's technical gaps and lead a practical development plan: mentoring, pairing, and learning routines;
- Conduct postmortems and map out the preventive action plan, with owners and deadlines defined;
- Connect the squad's technical needs with partner areas: Product, Infra, SRE, Data, and Architecture;
- Continuously align risks, technical priorities, and team development with the squad's Tech Manager and PM;
- Discuss with Architecture decisions with systemic impact (integration, data, security, scalability) and bring operational feedback into the evolution of the platform;
- Maintain consistency of standards, integration, and reuse together with the other Tech Leads;
- Take part in team ceremonies and discussions, supporting decision-making and conflict resolution.

**Expected Results:**

- Reduction in incidents caused by deployments and in the recurrence of the same type of failure;
- Increased quality: less rework, lower rollback rate, and lower bug leakage;
- Improved technical health: controlled technical debt, with a plan and continuous execution;
- Consistent observability: services with minimum dashboards and alerts, and SLOs defined where applicable;
- Team development: less dependence on the Tech Lead for day-to-day decisions, with more good decisions made by the group;
- Adherence to platform standards: reused building blocks and more predictable integrations;
- Measurable productivity gains from adopting AI in the development cycle.

