#### Job description

We are looking for a Mid-Level Planning Analyst to join our Planning team, focused on capacity management, forecasting, and performance of service operations.

We are looking for a professional with an analytical, organized, and data-driven profile, who has experience in multichannel service environments and is able to turn operational information into analyses that support decision-making and the proper sizing of operations.

**Main responsibilities**

Prepare and monitor Capacity Planning studies, considering demand, installed capacity, productivity, service levels, and operational needs;

Develop and monitor demand forecasts for service channels, identifying trends, seasonality, and deviations between forecast and actual results;

Perform sizing and capacity analyses for inbound service operations, covering Voice, Email, and digital channels;

Monitor and analyze operational indicators, such as SLA, AHT, Productivity, Absenteeism (ABS), volumes, capacity, and performance;

Identify performance deviations and carry out root cause analyses, proposing actions and recommendations to improve results;

Build scenarios and simulations to support decisions related to capacity, productivity, demand, and service levels;

Monitor alignment between forecasted demand, planned capacity, and actual results;

Prepare reports, dashboards, and management analyses that provide visibility into the main operational indicators;

Work in partnership with operational areas and other stakeholders, supporting discussions and decisions related to planning and performance;

Identify opportunities to improve and automate the area's processes and controls.

**Requirements**

Experience in Operations Planning / Workforce Management (WFM), preferably in customer service environments;

Strong knowledge of Capacity Planning and Forecasting;

Experience with inbound operations planning and multichannel environments, including Voice, Email, and digital channels;

Knowledge of key service indicators, such as SLA, AHT, Productivity, and Absenteeism;

Knowledge and experience with tools and environments such as Avaya, IVR, and Zendesk;

Ability to perform data analyses, identify deviations, and establish cause-and-effect relationships;

Advanced Excel, including mastery of formulas, pivot tables, handling large volumes of data, and building analyses;

Good analytical skills, logical reasoning, and attention to detail;

Good communication skills and the ability to translate technical analyses into clear information for different audiences.

**Knowledge considered a plus**

Python, especially for data analysis and routine automation;

Knowledge of databases and SQL;

Experience with Power BI, building dashboards and indicators;

Experience with process automation and handling large volumes of data;

Knowledge of Workforce Management methodologies and tools.

**Profile we are looking for**

We are looking for someone who has curiosity and ease working with numbers, but who goes beyond building reports. We expect a professional who can understand how operations behave, question results, identify causes, anticipate risks, and turn data into recommendations for the business.

It is important to have autonomy to lead analyses, organization to handle different demands, and ease interacting with operational areas and other stakeholders.

If you enjoy planning, data, and analysis, and understanding how demand, capacity, and performance connect to generate better results, this opportunity may be for you.

